- op: discuss  # f89c
  at: '2026-09-18T23:26:39Z'  # f89c
  by: agent  # f89c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f89c
  clock: 4  # f89c
  nonce: f89c  # f89c
  message: "Data point from the 2026-09-18 session-start hook: scripts/audit-autopr-convergence over 531 runs reports 58 violations — Class 1 (merged, then exit nonzero) 41, Class 2 (no declared terminal state) 17, of which THREE are post-instrumentation (post WI-nazoj) with 'abort site not recorded — set -u / bare exit / signal': 2026-09-18T03:57:46Z, 03:58:42Z, 04:00:35Z, all exit 1, PR number unrecorded, ~1 min apart. Not investigated in this session (WI-juzig was the task); the two auto-pr runs of this session both ended in a declared state (ci_failed exit 1 on #1065's first push — ARCHITECTURE.md freshness gate; merged exit 0 on the second). The three 03:57–04:00 rows are the next thing this row should look at: three runs in three minutes with no PR number reads like a retry loop dying before PR creation."  # f89c
- op: discuss  # 88c6
  at: '2026-09-20T20:51:26Z'  # 88c6
  by: agent  # 88c6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 88c6
  clock: 5  # 88c6
  nonce: 88c6  # 88c6
  message: "MEASURED 2026-09-20 on .git/AUTOPR_HISTORY.jsonl. 569 invocations; 84 post-instrumentation (first row carrying the abort_site key is 2026-09-16T04:52:18Z, commit 15a98292a1).\n\nTHE HEADLINE NUMBER, and it is not the one this item expected. The undeclared-terminal-state class is 22 of 84 post-instrumentation (26%). Pre-instrumentation it was 14 of 485 (2.9%). A 9x RISE, not a decline.\n\nTHE INSTRUMENT IS INERT. abort_site is non-null on ZERO of the 84 rows carrying the key. WI-nazoj's ERR trap has never once attributed an abort. Its own docstring names the three causes it cannot catch -- a set -u unbound variable, a bare exit, a signal -- so a uniformly-null column is not \"nothing went wrong\", it is \"every abort was of a kind this trap cannot see\".\n\nWHICH OF THE THREE, established behaviorally rather than by reading. A surviving run log (/tmp/autopr5.log, PR #1091, 2026-09-19T21:07) ends:\n\n    CONVERGENCE VIOLATION (INV-rahib / WI-nazoj)\n       auto-pr is exiting 1 with no declared terminal state.\n       Abort site: not recorded. ...\n    Terminated\n\n\"Terminated\" is the shell reporting SIGTERM. It is the third cause.\n\nTHE SOURCE OF THE SIGNAL, from the session transcript -- the invocation shape is\n\n    AUTO_PR_SKIP_MANIFEST=1 timeout 590 ./scripts/auto-pr --timeout 480\n\nThe agent wraps auto-pr in `timeout 590` because the harness caps one foreground Bash call at 600s. When CI outruns that budget, timeout SIGTERMs auto-pr mid-poll. The prior handoff recorded the outer code as 124 -- which is timeout's own \"I killed it\" code, not auto-pr's.\n\nREPRODUCED, both arms, on a 12-line fixture carrying auto-pr's trap structure (set -Eeuo pipefail, EXIT + ERR traps, terminal state declared after the poll):\n\n    external SIGTERM via timeout : final_state=unknown  abort_site=''  outer exit=124\n    control, allowed to finish   : final_state=merged   abort_site=''  outer exit=0\n\nArm 1 reproduces the ledger signature exactly, INCLUDING the two rows the audit singles out as \"exit 0 with no terminal state\" -- that is what a signal death records when the last command happened to return 0. Arm 2 is the non-vacuity control: the same fixture DOES record a state when allowed to finish.\n\nTHE ARITHMETIC MAKES IT STRUCTURAL, not bad luck. The CI poll default is 2400s and the 300s soft-retry is NOT optional (auto-pr:2152). Even `--timeout 240` commits to 540s of polling before Scenario B, plus push, PR-create, merge and cleanup. A blocking foreground auto-pr does not fit a 590s budget and cannot be made to.\n\nTHE WORK LANDED ANYWAY. Of the 15 distinct PRs behind the 22 rows, 14 are merged=true (ci-debug pr-status). The violation signal is firing on runs that SUCCEEDED and were finished by hand with merge-pr --wait-for-ci.\n\nRESIDUAL, so this is not read as \"all 22 explained\": PR #1079 is closed with merged=false, exit 0. Consistent with a Scenario B close-and-repush; not verified. I proved the mechanism, reproduced its exact signature, and showed the outcomes are consistent with it. I did NOT attribute each of the 22 rows individually."  # 88c6
